   164	### 2.3 Semantics (proposal; OB2 fixes them)
   165	
   166	- **Rmap.** Halpin's relational mapping. Each fact type with a compound
   167	  uniqueness constraint gets its own table. Fact types whose role is
   168	  functional on an entity are grouped into that entity's table. Reference
   169	  modes become key columns. 1:1 fact types are absorbed toward the mandatory
   170	  side. Subtypes are absorbed into the supertype unless they have their own
   171	  identification (D5). Objectified fact types become tables keyed by their
   172	  uniqueness. A fact type the rules cannot place is unmapped, with a closed
   173	  reason.
   174	- **Keys.** The primary uniqueness becomes `primary_key`. Every other
   175	  confirmed alethic uniqueness over one table's columns becomes a
   176	  `unique_keys` entry (D4).
   177	- **Relationships.** One per foreign key the Rmap produces, named
   178	  deterministically.
   179	- **Populations.** `sample_population` and `reference_populations` stay out of
   180	  every relational file and keep their `population:out-of-scope` refusal in
   181	  the loss report. A semantic model describes structure, not rows (D6).
   182	- **Unrepresentable constructs** (mandatory and NOT NULL, value constraints,
   183	  frequency, ring, subset, exclusion, derivations, deontic rules) are listed
   184	  in the mapping's `GND` extension by fact type or constraint id with a closed
   185	  reason. Nothing is dropped silently.
